  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Amarolide and SCCH-26 through a series of target interactions. Amarolide is implicated in targeting two entities: Hs746T and HaCaT, both of which are targets of Sophoradiol. Sophoradiol, in turn, is linked to SCCH-26, indicating a possible pathway where Amarolide may influence SCCH-26 via Sophoradiol. Similarly, Amarolide is also associated with HaCaT, which is targeted by a different compound, (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, which also targets SCCH-26. These findings suggest that Amarolide may exert its effects on SCCH-26 through multiple intermediate targets, possibly via different molecular mechanisms. The evidence is consistent with a role for Amarolide in modulating SCCH-26, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The scores from the different paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the evidence across the pathways.",
